    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "Consider team size and structure as quantitative thresholds. Organizations with fewer than 20-30 frontend engineers rarely justify micro-frontend complexity. Between 30-75 engineers, it depends heavily on team organization and product boundaries. Beyond 75-100 frontend engineers, especially when distributed across geographies or products, micro-frontends become increasingly attractive. These numbers aren't rigid rules-a 40-person team working on a highly modular product with clear boundaries might benefit, while a 60-person team on a tightly integrated application might not."
    }), "\n", "\n", _jsxs(_components.p, {
